@startuml
hide footbox
title Conditional static transaction scenario - runtime identity UNKNOWN
actor "Scenario entry" as Entry
participant "fixture.A" as B1
participant "fixture.B" as B2
legend left
All P identifiers are SYMBOLIC_SCENARIO; actual runtime identity UNKNOWN.
L = TRANSACTION_LOGICAL_SCOPE; P = TRANSACTION_PHYSICAL
S = TRANSACTION_SUSPENDED; SP = TRANSACTION_SAVEPOINT
Green: shared physical context / logical scope
Blue: independent physical scope; outer P retained while SUSPENDED
Yellow: nested SAVEPOINT on the SAME P
Gray: NO_TRANSACTION; red: UNKNOWN / unsupported path
Groups show method nesting. BEGIN/END notes define physical lifetimes.
Suspended lifetime overlap is explicit in SUSPEND/RESUME notes.
endlegend
Entry -> B1: fixture.A#outside() / CONDITIONAL_CALL
group #EEEEEE F1 UNANNOTATED METHOD_EXECUTION NO_TRANSACTION
note right of B1: proxy=SCENARIO_PROXY_CALL; manager=UNKNOWN_OR_NOT_USED
B1 -> B2: fixture.B#required() / CONDITIONAL_CALL
group #CCE5FF F2 REQUIRED L1 P1
note right of B2: proxy=SCENARIO_PROXY_CALL; manager=tx
note over B2: 3 PHYSICAL_BEGIN P1 
note over B2: 4 LOGICAL_BEGIN L1 
note over B2: 5 LOGICAL_END L1 
note over B2: 6 PHYSICAL_END_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN P1 
end
B2 --> B1: scope exit / outcome UNKNOWN
end
B1 --> Entry: scope exit / outcome UNKNOWN
@enduml
